      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nApply the existing `dflash` label to issue titles containing whole-word DFlash or DSpark, and recognize “spec decode” for `speculative-decoding`. Related: #62939 (labeling example only; this does not fix or close its startup bug).\n\n## Claims\n\n- Match DFlash and DSpark case-insensitively in issue titles using the existing whole-word keyword matcher.\n- Add “spec decode” alongside the existing speculative-decoding title phrases.\n- Preserve the shared `dflash` label established in #51459 and Ben Chislett’s [DSpark coverage feedback](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51459#discussion_r3770987282); no separate `dspark` label or PR-labeling changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node /private/tmp/vllm-issue-label-validation.cjs` — 389 cases passed, executing the actual workflow JavaScript with GitHub writes mocked. Includes #62939’s exact title, mixed/lower/upper capitalization, punctuation, longer-word negatives, unrelated titles, body-only negatives, existing labels, and comparison of every existing configured term in title/body against the baseline.\n- #62939’s title produces no labels before this patch and both `dflash` and `speculative-decoding` afterward.\n- `.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files .github/workflows/issue_autolabel.yml` — all applicable hooks passed, including actionlint.\n- YAML parsing and `git diff --check` — passed.\n- Model evaluation is not applicable: this changes only issue-labeling configuration, with no effect on model output, accuracy, or serving.\n\nThe JavaScript validation script is a local review artifact, not an additional repository change. The human submitter confirmed review and validation before submission.\n\n## Details\n\nThe issue workflow has no `dflash` rule, and its speculative-decoding phrases omit the shorthand used in #62939. This adds seven configuration lines and reuses the existing case-insensitive word-boundary and substring matching logic. Issue bodies remain excluded for these terms.\n\nDuplicate-work checks read #62939 and its comments, searched open PRs referencing it, and searched DFlash/DSpark labeling and issue-autolabel work. No open PR addresses this labeling gap. #63225 addresses the underlying startup failure; #62540 adds unrelated Reflection Beam labeling; #51459 is the merged predecessor establishing the intentional DFlash/DSpark grouping.\n\nAI assistance (OpenAI Codex) was used to apply the supplied patch, inspect prior feedback and duplicate work, run local validation, and prepare this PR.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
